1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,760
August, 1939. Europe is holding its breath.

2
00:00:05,560 --> 00:00:12,300
Hitler wants Poland. But he needs a reason.
Germany has to look like the victim, not the attacker.

3
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:18,990
So the SS comes up with a plan.
Its code name: Operation Konserve. Canned goods.

4
00:00:19,790 --> 00:00:24,610
Here, in the border town of Gleiwitz,
stands a German radio station.

5
00:00:25,410 --> 00:00:31,980
The idea is simple. SS men will dress in Polish uniforms
and attack their own station.

6
00:00:32,780 --> 00:00:40,100
They will fire a few shots at the walls
and broadcast a message in Polish: Poland is attacking Germany.

7
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:44,930
On the evening of August 31st, they do exactly that.

8
00:00:45,730 --> 00:00:50,400
The message goes on air. Almost no one hears it.
But that doesn't matter.

9
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:55,450
The signal to begin was a simple phrase:
"Grandmother is dead."

10
00:00:56,250 --> 00:01:03,330
At dawn on September 1st, the German army crosses the border.
The Second World War has begun.
